Guance.Windows.Native provides the CMake package GuanceWindowsNative:

    find_package(GuanceWindowsNative CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE Guance::WindowsNative)

The optional local diagnostics collector is enabled with the diagnostics feature:

    vcpkg install "guance-windows-native[diagnostics]:x64-windows"
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE Guance::Diagnostics)

Include guance_diagnostics.h. It uses the matching core DLL from this package;
collection remains off until guance_diagnostics_start(). Stop and close diagnostics
before unloading the collector DLL. Diagnostic stop does not flush business uploads.

Session Replay is an optional same-version DLL:

    vcpkg install "guance-windows-native[replay]:x64-windows"

Keep guance_windows_replay.dll adjacent to guance_windows_native.dll. Existing
Replay configuration and C API calls remain unchanged. When Replay is enabled
without the DLL, the core reports one component diagnostic and continues RUM.

Install the JavaScript adapter with npm for both Electron modes:

    npm install @cloudcare/electron-native-adapter

Mixed Mode reuses an SDK Handle owned by the application. Install the base
native package:

    vcpkg install "guance-windows-native:x64-windows"

Include guance_sdk.h, start guance_electron_bridge_server_start() with the
existing guance_sdk_handle, and use the npm package's public entry points:

    @cloudcare/electron-native-adapter
    @cloudcare/electron-native-adapter/preload/standalone
    @cloudcare/electron-native-adapter/preload/install

New Full Mode applications obtain the Bridge EXE and DLL through the
bundled native/win32-x64 directory in @cloudcare/electron-native-adapter. No vcpkg is required.
Call bootstrap(managed) or startFullMode() without a native directory and stage the
runtime outside ASAR with @cloudcare/electron-native-adapter/packaging/windows.

The following legacy Full Mode feature is deprecated but retained for transition:

    vcpkg install "guance-windows-native[electron-bridge]:x64-windows"

The feature installs only the EXE plus its adjacent runtime under
tools/guance-windows-native. Use startFullMode() from the npm package's public
Main Process entry point; do not launch private protocol modules directly.

The port supports dynamic x64-windows. Session Replay is experimental, opt-in,
and disabled by default at runtime. The npm adapter exposes Browser RUM's records
capability only when the native Replay component is installed and enabled.
The port has no default SQLite
dependency and does not install JavaScript files.
